Print "Testing Pure Simple English Syntax..."

Set colors to a list of "red", "green" and "blue"
Assert Length(colors) == 3, "Colors length should be 3"
Assert colors[0] == "red", "First color should be red"

Add "yellow" to colors
Assert Length(colors) == 4, "Colors length should be 4 after Add"
Assert colors[3] == "yellow", "Appended color should be yellow"

Set empty_box to an empty list
Assert empty_box is empty, "empty_box should be empty"
Assert Length(empty_box) == 0, "Length of empty_box should be 0"

Set car to an object with:
    make: "Tesla"
    model: "Model S"
    year: 2024
    electric: true

Assert car.make == "Tesla", "Car make"
Assert car.year == 2024, "Car year"
Assert car.electric is true, "Car electric"

Set config to an empty object
Assert Keys(config) is empty, "Config keys should be empty"

Set balance to 500
Assert balance is positive, "Balance should be positive"
Assert balance is not negative, "Balance should not be negative"

Set debt to - 50
Assert debt is negative, "Debt should be negative"

Set zero_val to 0
Assert zero_val is zero, "Zero should be zero"

Set even_num to 42
Assert even_num is even, "42 should be even"
Assert even_num is not odd, "42 should not be odd"

Set odd_num to 17
Assert odd_num is odd, "17 should be odd"

Set missing_val to nothing
Assert missing_val is nothing, "missing_val should be nothing"

Set present_val to "Hello"
Assert present_val is something, "present_val should be something"

Set counter to 0
Do 5 times:
    Increase counter by 1
Assert counter == 5, "Repeat counter should be 5"

Set found_blue to false
For every c in colors:
    If c is equal to "blue":
        Set found_blue to true
        Stop the loop
Assert found_blue is true, "Should have stopped after finding blue"

Create a function called multiply with a and b:
    Give back a * b

Set prod to multiply(6, 7)
Assert prod == 42, "6 * 7 should be 42"

Create a function called void_fn:
    Return nothing

Assert void_fn() is nothing, "Void fn should return nothing"

Set called_val to 0
Create a function called record_val with v:
    Set called_val to v

Call record_val with 99
Assert called_val == 99, "Call record_val should set called_val to 99"

Print "All Simple English language tests passed successfully!"
